i don't understand how would you know when the vars for the first subtask end and the vars for the second subtask begin

suppose you have
func = function (a1,a2,a3,a4,a5)
 {...
}

will the internal.func1 use a1,a2,a3  leaving a4 and a5 to internal.func2? or maybe just use a1,a2 for internal.func1?

the obvious solution is to encapsulate the parameters in lists. you have
funct = function(list1,list2) {
...
internal.func1(list1)
internal.func2(list2)
...
}

with each list containing as many parameters as you want.

